      "text": "80-year-old female presenting with knee pain for 3 years. Character: stiffness with cracking sound; radiation: to the calf; aggravated by sitting on the floor; relieved by oil massage. Severity 7/10. Associated: swelling, difficulty walking. PMH: Hypertension for 14 years; Hypothyroidism for 7 years. Drugs: Amlodipine 5 mg; Levothyroxine 50 mcg. Allergy: no known allergies. Family: heart disease. Personal: smokes bidi daily. Triage: ROUTINE."
